3. Mathematical Model

3.1 Latent dynamics

Let

[
X_t\in\mathcal X\subseteq\mathbb R^n,
\qquad
U_t\in\mathcal U\subseteq\mathbb R^p.
]

The latent dynamics are

[
X_{t+1}

F_\theta(X_t,U_t)+\eta_t,
\tag{3}
]

with

[
\eta_t\sim P_{\eta,\theta}.
]

For the Gaussian special case,

[
\eta_t\sim\mathcal N(0,\Sigma_\eta).
]

---

3.2 Intervention-sensitive observation model

The observable variable satisfies

[
Y_t

h_\phi(X_t,U_t)+\epsilon_t,
\tag{4}
]

with

[
\epsilon_t\sim P_{\epsilon,\phi}.
]

In the Gaussian case,

[
\epsilon_t\sim\mathcal N(0,\Sigma_\epsilon).
]

The Jacobian of the observation function decomposes into two conceptually distinct sensitivities:

[
D_Xh_\phi
]

and

[
D_Uh_\phi.
]

The first describes sensitivity to the latent state.

The second describes direct intervention-induced measurement distortion.

The problematic regime is

[
\boxed{
D_Uh_\phi\neq0.
}
]

