4. Candidate Model Space

Define the candidate model as

[
M=
(\theta,\phi,\Sigma_\eta,\Sigma_\epsilon)
\in\mathcal M.
\tag{5}
]

More generally, one may write

[
M=(G,\theta,F_\theta,h_\phi,\Sigma),
]

where G represents the causal structure.

The admissible model set after observing data \mathcal D_t under interventions U is

