15. Definition 4: Local Diagnostic Decoupling Ratio

For

[
v\in T_U\mathcal U,
\qquad
|v|=1,
]

define

[
\boxed{
\rho(v;X,U)

\frac{
|D_Uh_\phi(X,U)v|{\mathcal Y}
}{
|D_UF\theta(X,U)v|_{\mathcal X}
+\lambda
}
}
\tag{22}
]

with

[
\lambda>0.
]

The regularization parameter prevents singular behavior when

[
D_UF,v=0.
]

Define

[
\rho^\star(X,U)

\sup_{|v|\le1}\rho(v;X,U).
\tag{23}
]

A direction v^\star is \rho_{\mathrm{crit}}-diagnostic if

[
\rho(v^\star;X,U)
\ge
\rho_{\mathrm{crit}}.
\tag{24}
]

If

[
\rho^\star<\rho_{\mathrm{crit}},
]

then the system is locally non-decouplable under the specified intervention class.

---

16. Why \rho Alone Is Not an Identifiability Criterion

The ratio \rho measures channel separation.

It does not establish that the latent state is observable.

A direction can strongly perturb Y while carrying no information about a target component of X.

Thus:

[
\boxed{
\text{Diagnostic decoupling}
\neq
\text{latent identifiability}.
}
]

This distinction is the reason a second condition is required.

---

17. Dynamically Induced Observability

Let the continuous-time analogue be

[
\dot X=F_\theta(X,U).
]

For an output

[
Y=h_\phi(X,U),
]

the nonlinear observability codistribution is generated by

[
dh,
\quad
dL_Fh,
\quad
dL_F^2h,
\ldots
]

where L_F denotes the Lie derivative along F.

For discrete-time systems, the corresponding construction is obtained from successive compositions of the state-transition and observation maps.

The crucial point is that diagnostic information may enter an initially unobservable latent direction only after being propagated through the dynamics.

Therefore, the relevant object is not simply

[
dh,
]

but the dynamically generated family

[
\mathcal O_F(h)

\operatorname{span}
\left{
dh,
dL_Fh,
dL_F^2h,\ldots
\right}.
\tag{25}
]

---

18. Target-Relevant Observability

Full state observability is stronger than necessary when only a target functional is required.

Let

[
T:\mathcal X\rightarrow\mathbb R^q.
]

The target is locally observable if

[
\operatorname{span}(dT)
\subseteq
\mathcal O_F(h).
\tag{26}
]

For scalar T,

[
\operatorname{rank}(dT)=1.
]

For complete state identification,

[
\operatorname{rank}\mathcal O_F(h)=n.
]

The target-relevant formulation is preferable because the controller need not reconstruct every latent degree of freedom if only a particular functional matters.

