20. The Corrected Structural Requirement

The diagnostic perturbation must satisfy two distinct requirements.

Requirement I: Channel Separation

There must exist a direction v^\star satisfying

[
|D_Uh,v^\star|
\gg
|D_UF,v^\star|.
\tag{28}
]

This allows estimation of the direct intervention-to-proxy pathway.

Requirement II: Target-Relevant Dynamic Excitation

The intervention must also excite latent directions that are relevant to T and observable through the subsequent system evolution.

This requires a rank condition involving

[
D_UF,v^\star
]

and the dynamically propagated observation derivatives.

---

