For vector-valued targets, however, this scalar rank comparison is insufficient by itself.

The stronger requirement is target distinguishability:

[
dT,\delta X\neq0
]

must imply that \delta X is distinguishable through the diagnostic observation sequence.

Equivalently, the target-sensitive subspace must not be contained in the dynamically unobservable subspace.

