one has either

[
\rho(v)<\rho_{\mathrm{crit}}
]

or

[
\ker\mathscr O_K(v)
\cap
{\delta X:dT(X)\delta X\neq0}
\neq\varnothing.
]

Then the available intervention class cannot guarantee target identification through the specified proxy.

Therefore:

[
\boxed{
\text{No admissible target-relevant excitation}
\Rightarrow
\text{no guaranteed proxy-control identification}.
}
]

This is an important negative result.

The framework therefore does not promise that every proxy can be made useful by sufficiently clever control.

Some observation structures are fundamentally insufficient.

