32. Necessary Versus Sufficient Conditions

A major objective of Gate 1 is to distinguish:

Necessary conditions

Conditions that must hold for identification to be possible.

For example:

[
\Gamma_{\mathrm{PC}}=0
]

is necessary for exact identification within the specified model class.

Likewise, if

[
dT
]

lies entirely inside a persistent unobservable subspace, target identification is impossible.

Sufficient conditions

Conditions under which an identification guarantee can actually be proven.

The proposed package is:

[
\boxed{
\text{Diagnostic separation}
+
\text{persistent excitation}
+
\text{target-relative observability}
+
\text{consistent estimation}.
}
]

The distinction is critical.

A rank condition that merely looks plausible should not be promoted to a theorem until sufficiency is demonstrated.

